^YTT(601.712,45,1,1,0)="{""name"": ""GDS DEMENTIA"", "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,2,0)=" ""copyright"": ""Copyright (c) 1983 by Barry Reisberg, M.D."", "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,3,0)=" ""restartDays"": 2, "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,4,0)=" ""printTitle"": ""Global Deterioration Scale"","
^YTT(601.712,45,1,5,0)=" ""content"":["
^YTT(601.712,45,1,6,0)="   {""id"": ""q3933"", ""type"": ""ChoiceQuestion"", ""required"": false, ""inline"": false, "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,7,0)="    ""text"": "" <strong>Global Deterioration Scale</strong><br /><br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,8,0)=" 1. No cognitive decline<br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,9,0)=" No subjective complaints of memory deficit. No memory deficit evident on"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,10,0)=" clinical interview.<br /><br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,11,0)=" 2. Very mild cognitive decline (Age Associated Memory Impairment)<br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,12,0)=" Subjective complaints of memory deficit, most frequently in following areas: (a)"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,13,0)=" forgetting where one has placed familiar objects; (b) forgetting names one"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,14,0)=" formerly knew well. No objective evidence of memory deficit on clinical"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,15,0)=" interview. No objective deficits in employment or social situations. Appropriate"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,16,0)=" concern with respect to symptomatology.<br /><br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,17,0)=" 3. Mild cognitive decline (Mild Cognitive Impairment)<br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,18,0)=" Earliest clear-cut deficits. Manifestations in more than one of the following areas:"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,19,0)=" (a) patient may have gotten lost when traveling to an unfamiliar location; (b) coworkers"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,20,0)=" become aware of patient''s relatively poor performance; (c) word and"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,21,0)=" name finding deficit becomes evident to intimates; (d) patient may read a passage"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,22,0)=" or a book and retain relatively little material; (e) patient may demonstrate"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,23,0)=" decreased facility in remembering names upon introduction to new people; (f)"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,24,0)=" patient may have lost or misplaced an object of value; (g) concentration deficit"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,25,0)=" may be evident on clinical testing. Objective evidence of memory deficit obtained"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,26,0)=" only with an intensive interview. Decreased performance in demanding"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,27,0)=" employment and social settings. Denial begins to become manifest in patient."
^YTT(601.712,45,1,28,0)=" Mild to moderate anxiety accompanies symptoms.<br /><br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,29,0)=" 4. Moderate cognitive decline (Mild Dementia)<br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,30,0)=" Clear-cut deficit on careful clinical interview. Deficit manifest in following areas:"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,31,0)=" (a) decreased knowledge of current and recent events; (b) may exhibit some"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,32,0)=" deficit in memory of ones personal history; (c) concentration deficit elicited on"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,33,0)=" serial subtractions; (d) decreased ability to travel, handle finances, etc. Frequently"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,34,0)=" no deficit in following areas: (a) orientation to time and place; (b) recognition of"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,35,0)=" familiar persons and faces; (c) ability to travel to familiar locations. Inability to"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,36,0)=" perform complex tasks. Denial is dominant defense mechanism. Flattening of"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,37,0)=" affect and withdrawal from challenging situations frequently occur.<br /><br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,38,0)=" 5. Moderately severe cognitive decline (Moderate Dementia)<br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,39,0)=" Patient can no longer survive without some assistance. Patient is unable during"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,40,0)=" interview to recall a major relevant aspect of their current lives, e.g., an address or"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,41,0)=" telephone number of many years, the names of close family members (such as"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,42,0)=" grandchildren), the name of the high school or college from which they"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,43,0)=" graduated. Frequently some disorientation to time (date, day of week, season)"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,44,0)=" or to place. An educated person may have difficulty counting back from 40"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,45,0)=" by 4s or from 20 by 2s. Persons at this stage retain knowledge of many major"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,46,0)=" facts regarding themselves and others. They invariably know their own names"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,47,0)=" and generally know their spouses' and children's names. They require no"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,48,0)=" assistance with toileting and eating, but may have some difficulty choosing the"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,49,0)=" proper clothing to wear.<br /><br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,50,0)=" 6. Severe cognitive decline (Moderately Severe Dementia)<br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,51,0)=" May occasionally forget the name of the spouse upon whom they are entirely"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,52,0)=" dependent for survival. Will be largely unaware of all recent events and"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,53,0)=" experiences in their lives. Retain some knowledge of their past lives but this is"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,54,0)=" very sketchy. Generally unaware of their surroundings, the year, the season, etc."
^YTT(601.712,45,1,55,0)=" May have difficulty counting from 10, both backward and, sometimes, forward."
^YTT(601.712,45,1,56,0)=" Will require some assistance with activities of daily living, e.g., may become"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,57,0)=" incontinent, will require travel assistance but occasionally will be able to travel to"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,58,0)=" familiar locations. Diurnal rhythm frequently disturbed. Almost always recall"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,59,0)=" their own name. Frequently continue to be able to distinguish familiar from"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,60,0)=" unfamiliar persons in their environment. Personality and emotional changes"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,61,0)=" occur. These are quite variable and include: (a) delusional behavior, e.g., patients"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,62,0)=" may accuse their spouse of being an impostor, may talk to imaginary figures in"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,63,0)=" the environment, or to their own reflection in the mirror; (b) obsessive symptoms,"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,64,0)=" e.g., person may continually repeat simple cleaning activities; (c) anxiety"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,65,0)=" symptoms, agitation, and even previously nonexistent violent behavior may"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,66,0)=" occur; (d) cognitive abulla, i.e., loss of willpower because an individual cannot"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,67,0)=" carry a thought long enough to determine a purposeful course of action.<br /><br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,68,0)=" 7. Very severe cognitive decline (Severe Dementia)<br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,69,0)=" All verbal abilities are lost over the course of this stage. Frequently there is no"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,70,0)=" speech at all - only unintelligible utterances and rare emergence of seemingly"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,71,0)=" forgotten words and phrases. Incontinent of urine, requires assistance toileting"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,72,0)=" and feeding. Basic psychomotor skills, e.g., ability to walk, are lost with the"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,73,0)=" progression of this stage. The brain appears to no longer be able to tell the body"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,74,0)=" what to do. Generalized rigidity and developmental neurologic reflexes are"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,75,0)=" frequently present.<br /><br />"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,76,0)=" Select the category that fits the patient best, most of the time."", "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,77,0)="    ""columns"": 1, "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,78,0)="    ""choices"":["
^YTT(601.712,45,1,79,0)="     {""id"": ""c2381"", ""text"": ""1. No cognitive decline"", ""quickKey"": 1}, "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,80,0)="     {""id"": ""c2382"", ""text"": ""2. Very mild cognitive decline---Forgetful"", ""quickKey"": 2}, "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,81,0)="     {""id"": ""c2383"", ""text"": ""3. Mild cognitive decline---Early confusional"", ""quickKey"": 3}, "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,82,0)="     {""id"": ""c2384"", ""text"": ""4. Moderate cognitive decline---Late confusional"", ""quickKey"": 4}, "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,83,0)="     {""id"": ""c2385"", ""text"": ""5. Moderately severe cognitive decline---Early dementia"", ""quickKey"": 5}, "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,84,0)="     {""id"": ""c2386"", ""text"": ""6. Severe cognitive decline---Middle dementia"", ""quickKey"": 6}, "
^YTT(601.712,45,1,85,0)="     {""id"": ""c2387"", ""text"": ""7. Very severe cognitive decline---Late dementia"", ""quickKey"": 7}"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,86,0)="   ]}]"
^YTT(601.712,45,1,87,0)="}"
^YTT(601.712,46,0)="153^3220408.085505^1831630262"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,0)="^^93^93^3220408"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,1,0)="{""name"": ""CDR"", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,2,0)=" ""restartDays"": 2, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,3,0)=" ""printTitle"": ""Clinical Dementia Rating"","
^YTT(601.712,46,1,4,0)=" ""content"":["
^YTT(601.712,46,1,5,0)="   {""id"": ""i395"", ""type"": ""IntroText"", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,6,0)="    ""text"": ""Score only as decline from previous usual level due to cognitive loss, not"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,7,0)=" impairment due to other factors.  """
^YTT(601.712,46,1,8,0)="    }, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,9,0)="   {""id"": ""q3903"", ""type"": ""ChoiceQuestion"", ""required"": false, ""inline"": false, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,10,0)="    ""text"": ""1. Memory"", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,11,0)="    ""intro"": ""Score only as decline from previous usual level due to cognitive loss, not"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,12,0)=" impairment due to other factors.  "", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,13,0)="    ""columns"": 1, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,14,0)="    ""choices"":["
^YTT(601.712,46,1,15,0)="     {""id"": ""c2630"", ""text"": ""0. No memory loss or slight inconsistent forgetfulness"", ""quickKey"": 0}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,16,0)="     {""id"": ""c2631"", ""text"": ""1. Consistent slight forgetfulness; partial recollection of events;"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,17,0)=" \u0022benign\u0022 forgetfulness"", ""quickKey"": 1}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,18,0)="     {""id"": ""c2632"", ""text"": ""2. Moderate memory loss; more marked for recent events; defect interferes with"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,19,0)=" everyday activities"", ""quickKey"": 2}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,20,0)="     {""id"": ""c2633"", ""text"": ""3. Severe memory loss; only highly learned material retained; new material"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,21,0)=" rapidly lost"", ""quickKey"": 3}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,22,0)="     {""id"": ""c2634"", ""text"": ""4. Severe memory loss; only fragments remain"", ""quickKey"": 4}"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,23,0)="   ]}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,24,0)="   {""id"": ""q3904"", ""type"": ""ChoiceQuestion"", ""required"": false, ""inline"": false, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,25,0)="    ""text"": ""2. Orientation"", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,26,0)="    ""intro"": ""Score only as decline from previous usual level due to cognitive loss, not"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,27,0)=" impairment due to other factors.  "", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,28,0)="    ""columns"": 1, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,29,0)="    ""choices"":["
^YTT(601.712,46,1,30,0)="     {""id"": ""c2635"", ""text"": ""0. Fully oriented"", ""quickKey"": 0}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,31,0)="     {""id"": ""c2636"", ""text"": ""1. Fully oriented except for slight difficulty with time relationships"", ""quickKey"": 1}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,32,0)="     {""id"": ""c2637"", ""text"": ""2. Moderate difficulty with time relationships; oriented for place at"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,33,0)=" examination; may have geographic disorientation elsewhere"", ""quickKey"": 2}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,34,0)="     {""id"": ""c2638"", ""text"": ""3. Severe difficulty with time relationships; usually disoriented to time, often"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,35,0)=" to place"", ""quickKey"": 3}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,36,0)="     {""id"": ""c2639"", ""text"": ""4. Oriented to person only"", ""quickKey"": 4}"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,37,0)="   ]}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,38,0)="   {""id"": ""q3905"", ""type"": ""ChoiceQuestion"", ""required"": false, ""inline"": false, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,39,0)="    ""text"": ""3. Judgment and Problem Solving"", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,40,0)="    ""intro"": ""Score only as decline from previous usual level due to cognitive loss, not"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,41,0)=" impairment due to other factors.  "", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,42,0)="    ""columns"": 1, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,43,0)="    ""choices"":["
^YTT(601.712,46,1,44,0)="     {""id"": ""c2659"", ""text"": ""0. Solves everyday problems; handles business and financial affairs well;"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,45,0)=" judgment good in relation to past performance"", ""quickKey"": 0}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,46,0)="     {""id"": ""c2641"", ""text"": ""1. Slight impairment in solving problems, similarities, and differences"", ""quickKey"": 1}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,47,0)="     {""id"": ""c2642"", ""text"": ""2. Moderate difficulty in handling problems, similarities, and differences;"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,48,0)=" social judgment usually maintained"", ""quickKey"": 2}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,49,0)="     {""id"": ""c2643"", ""text"": ""3. Severely impaired in handling problems, similarities, and differences; social"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,50,0)=" judgment usually impaired"", ""quickKey"": 3}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,51,0)="     {""id"": ""c2644"", ""text"": ""4. Unable to make judgments or solve problems"", ""quickKey"": 4}"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,52,0)="   ]}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,53,0)="   {""id"": ""q3906"", ""type"": ""ChoiceQuestion"", ""required"": false, ""inline"": false, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,54,0)="    ""text"": ""4. Community Affairs"", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,55,0)="    ""intro"": ""Score only as decline from previous usual level due to cognitive loss, not"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,56,0)=" impairment due to other factors.  "", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,57,0)="    ""columns"": 1, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,58,0)="    ""choices"":["
^YTT(601.712,46,1,59,0)="     {""id"": ""c2645"", ""text"": ""0. Independent function at usual level in job, shopping, volunteer and social"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,60,0)=" groups"", ""quickKey"": 0}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,61,0)="     {""id"": ""c2646"", ""text"": ""1. Slight impairment in these activities"", ""quickKey"": 1}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,62,0)="     {""id"": ""c2647"", ""text"": ""2. Unable to function independently at these activities although may still be"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,63,0)=" engaged in some; appears normal to casual inspection"", ""quickKey"": 2}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,64,0)="     {""id"": ""c2648"", ""text"": ""3. No pretense of independent function outside home: Appears well enough to be"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,65,0)=" taken to functions outside a family home"", ""quickKey"": 3}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,66,0)="     {""id"": ""c2649"", ""text"": ""4. No pretense of independent function outside home: Appears too ill to be taken"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,67,0)=" to functions outside a family home"", ""quickKey"": 4}"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,68,0)="   ]}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,69,0)="   {""id"": ""q3907"", ""type"": ""ChoiceQuestion"", ""required"": false, ""inline"": false, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,70,0)="    ""text"": ""5. Home and Hobbies"", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,71,0)="    ""intro"": ""Score only as decline from previous usual level due to cognitive loss, not"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,72,0)=" impairment due to other factors.  "", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,73,0)="    ""columns"": 1, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,74,0)="    ""choices"":["
^YTT(601.712,46,1,75,0)="     {""id"": ""c2650"", ""text"": ""0. Life at home, hobbies, and intellectual interests well maintained"", ""quickKey"": 0}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,76,0)="     {""id"": ""c2651"", ""text"": ""1. Life at home, hobbies, and intellectual interests slightly impaired"", ""quickKey"": 1}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,77,0)="     {""id"": ""c2652"", ""text"": ""2. Mild but definite impairment of function at home; more difficult chores"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,78,0)=" abandoned; more complicated hobbies and interests abandoned"", ""quickKey"": 2}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,79,0)="     {""id"": ""c2653"", ""text"": ""3. Only simple chores preserved; very restricted interests, poorly maintained"", ""quickKey"": 3}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,80,0)="     {""id"": ""c2654"", ""text"": ""4. No significant function in home"", ""quickKey"": 4}"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,81,0)="   ]}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,82,0)="   {""id"": ""q3908"", ""type"": ""ChoiceQuestion"", ""required"": false, ""inline"": false, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,83,0)="    ""text"": ""6. Personal Care"", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,84,0)="    ""intro"": ""Score only as decline from previous usual level due to cognitive loss, not"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,85,0)=" impairment due to other factors.  "", "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,86,0)="    ""columns"": 1, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,87,0)="    ""choices"":["
^YTT(601.712,46,1,88,0)="     {""id"": ""c2655"", ""text"": ""0. Fully capable of self-care"", ""quickKey"": 0}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,89,0)="     {""id"": ""c2656"", ""text"": ""1. Needs prompting"", ""quickKey"": 1}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,90,0)="     {""id"": ""c2657"", ""text"": ""2. Requires assistance in dressing, hygiene, keeping of personal effects"", ""quickKey"": 2}, "
^YTT(601.712,46,1,91,0)="     {""id"": ""c2658"", ""text"": ""3. Requires much help with personal care; frequent incontinence"", ""quickKey"": 3}"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,92,0)="   ]}]"
^YTT(601.712,46,1,93,0)="}"
^YTT(601.712,47,0)="154^3221219.204427^3397187901"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,0)="^^64^64^3230706"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,1,0)="{""name"": ""FAST"", "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,2,0)=" ""copyright"": ""Copyright  (c) 1984 by Barry Reisberg, M.D."", "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,3,0)=" ""restartDays"": 2, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,4,0)=" ""printTitle"": ""Functional Assessment Staging"", "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,5,0)=" ""content"":["
^YTT(601.712,47,1,6,0)="   {""id"": ""i2473"", ""type"": ""IntroText"", "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,7,0)="    ""text"": ""The FAST scale is a functional scale designed to evaluate patients at the"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,8,0)=" moderate-severe stages of dementia. In the early stages the patient may be able"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,9,0)=" to participate in the FAST administration but usually the information should be"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,10,0)=" collected from a caregiver or, in the case of nursing home care, the nursing"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,11,0)=" home staff. The FAST Stage is the highest consecutive level of disability.  For"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,12,0)=" clinical purposes, in addition to staging the level of disability, additional,"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,13,0)=" non-ordinal (nonconsecutive) deficits should be noted, since these additional"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,14,0)=" deficits are of clear clinical relevance."""
^YTT(601.712,47,1,15,0)="    }, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,16,0)="   {""id"": ""q8788"", ""type"": ""ChoiceQuestion"", ""required"": true, ""inline"": false, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,17,0)="    ""text"": ""1. Check the highest consecutive level of disability:"", "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,18,0)="    ""intro"": ""The FAST scale is a functional scale designed to evaluate patients at the"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,19,0)=" moderate-severe stages of dementia. In the early stages the patient may be able"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,20,0)=" to participate in the FAST administration but usually the information should be"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,21,0)=" collected from a caregiver or, in the case of nursing home care, the nursing"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,22,0)=" home staff. The FAST Stage is the highest consecutive level of disability.  For"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,23,0)=" clinical purposes, in addition to staging the level of disability, additional,"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,24,0)=" non-ordinal (nonconsecutive) deficits should be noted, since these additional"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,25,0)=" deficits are of clear clinical relevance."", "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,26,0)="    ""columns"": 1, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,27,0)="    ""choices"":["
^YTT(601.712,47,1,28,0)="     {""id"": ""c5335"", ""text"": "" 1 No difficulty, either subjectively or objectively.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,29,0)="     {""id"": ""c5336"", ""text"": "" 2 Complains of forgetting location of objects. Subjective work difficulties.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,30,0)="     {""id"": ""c5337"", ""text"": "" 3 Decreased job functioning evident to co-workers.  Difficulty in traveling to"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,31,0)=" new locations.  Decreased organizational capacity.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,32,0)="     {""id"": ""c5338"", ""text"": "" 4 Decreased ability to perform complex tasks, e.g. planning dinner for guests,"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,33,0)=" handling personal finances (such as forgetting to pay bills), difficulty"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,34,0)=" marketing, etc.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,35,0)="     {""id"": ""c5339"", ""text"": "" 5 Requires assistance in choosing proper clothing to wear for the day, season,"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,36,0)=" or occasion, e.g. patient may wear the same clothing repeatedly, unless"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,37,0)=" supervised.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,38,0)="     {""id"": ""c5340"", ""text"": "" 6a Improperly putting on clothes without assistance or cuing (e.g. may put"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,39,0)=" street clothes on over night clothes, or put shoes on wrong feet, or have"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,40,0)=" difficulty buttoning clothing) occasionally or more frequently over the past"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,41,0)=" weeks.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,42,0)="     {""id"": ""c5341"", ""text"": "" 6b Unable to bathe (shower) properly (e.g., difficulty adjusting bath-water"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,43,0)=" (shower) temperature) occasionally or more frequently over the past weeks.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,44,0)="     {""id"": ""c5342"", ""text"": "" 6c Inability to handle mechanics of toileting (e.g., forgets to flush the"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,45,0)=" toilet, does not wipe properly or properly dispose of toilet tissue)"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,46,0)=" occasionally or more frequently over the past weeks.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,47,0)="     {""id"": ""c5343"", ""text"": "" 6d Urinary incontinence (occasionally or more frequently over the past weeks).""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,48,0)="     {""id"": ""c5344"", ""text"": "" 6e Fecal incontinence (occasionally or more frequently over the past weeks).""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,49,0)="     {""id"": ""c5345"", ""text"": "" 7a Ability to speak limited to approximately a half a dozen intelligible"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,50,0)=" different words or fewer, in the course of an average day or in the course of an"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,51,0)=" intensive interview.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,52,0)="     {""id"": ""c5346"", ""text"": "" 7b Speech ability limited to the use of a single intelligible word in an average"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,53,0)=" day or in the course of an interview (the person may repeat the word over and"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,54,0)=" over).""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,55,0)="     {""id"": ""c5347"", ""text"": "" 7c Ambulatory ability lost (cannot walk without personal assistance).""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,56,0)="     {""id"": ""c5348"", ""text"": "" 7d Cannot sit up without assistance (e.g., the individual will fall over if"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,57,0)=" there are no lateral rests [arms] on the chair).""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,58,0)="     {""id"": ""c5349"", ""text"": "" 7e Loss of ability to smile.""}, "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,59,0)="     {""id"": ""c5350"", ""text"": "" 7f Loss of ability to hold up head independently.""}"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,60,0)="   ]}], "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,61,0)=" ""rules"":["
^YTT(601.712,47,1,62,0)="   {""question"": ""q3909"", ""operator"": ""EQ"", ""value"": ""c241"", "
^YTT(601.712,47,1,63,0)="    ""skips"":[""q3916"",""q3917"",""q3918"",""q3919"",""q3920"",""q3921"",""q3922"",""q3923"",""q3924"",""q3925"",""q3926"",""q3927"",""q3928"",""q3929"",""q3932""]}]"
^YTT(601.712,47,1,64,0)="}"
