^YTT(601.712,148,1,21,0)=" participate in the FAST administration but usually the information should be"
^YTT(601.712,148,1,22,0)=" collected from a caregiver or, in the case of nursing home care, the nursing"
^YTT(601.712,148,1,23,0)=" home staff. The FAST Stage is the highest consecutive level of disability.  For"
^YTT(601.712,148,1,24,0)=" clinical purposes, in addition to staging the level of disability, additional,"
^YTT(601.712,148,1,25,0)=" non-ordinal (nonconsecutive) deficits should be noted, since these additional"
